{#
/**
 * @file
 * The component editor's form layout.
 *
 * Three bands in a column: a pinned header, the fields, and a pinned footer.
 * The middle band is the only thing that scrolls.
 *
 * This exists because the shared `entity_edit_form` template renders the header
 * *inside* the two-column row, which is right for a page that scrolls as a
 * whole and wrong here. With the header inside the scroller it has to pin
 * itself with `position: sticky`, and then anything else wanting to pin — an
 * array's legend carrying its pager, say — has to offset itself by a header
 * height that changes with the active tab. Taking the header out of the
 * scroller removes that whole class of arithmetic: `top: 0` means the top.
 *
 * `layout-entity-form` is kept so the form still picks up the shared entity
 * form styling; only the arrangement differs.
 *
 * Alchemist folds `actions` into `footer` itself, and has no `advanced`
 * sidebar, but both are rendered here so this stays a complete layout rather
 * than one that silently drops a region if that ever changes.
 *
 * @see \Drupal\neo_alchemist\Form\InstanceComponentForm::claimFormTheme()
 * @see neo_back/templates/entity-edit-form.html.twig
 */
#}
<div class="layout-entity-form neo-alchemist--form-layout">
  {{ form.header }}
  <div class="neo-alchemist--form-body">
    <div class="py-4">
      {{ form|without('header', 'advanced', 'footer', 'actions') }}
      {% if form.advanced %}
        {{ form.advanced|neo_class('layout-entity-form--advanced mt-form-item') }}
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="border-t -mx-form-item p-form-item">
    {{ form.footer }}
    {{ form.actions }}
  </div>
</div>
